// A bandit shakedown - the conversation-player test scene, written in Yarn.
// The same scene is in shakedown.ink, so the two languages can be read side by side.
//
// gold() is a question the game answers. <<TakeMoney>> and <<ChangeStanding>> are actions
// the game carries out. $asked_about_road is Yarn's own memory, local to this conversation.
// Each #line: tag is the line's id - what crosses the network, and what a translation keys on.

title: Shakedown
---
<<declare $asked_about_road = false>>
Bandit: Toll road. Twenty gold, or you walk back the way you came. #line:shakedown_toll
<<jump Choices>>
===

title: Choices
---
-> Pay the toll. <<if gold() >= 20>> #line:shakedown_pay
    <<TakeMoney 20>>
    Bandit: Pleasure doing business. Road's yours. #line:shakedown_paid
-> Who says it's your road? <<if not $asked_about_road>> #line:shakedown_ask
    <<set $asked_about_road to true>>
    Bandit: The twelve of us in those rocks say so. #line:shakedown_twelve
    <<jump Choices>>
-> Get out of my way. #line:shakedown_refuse
    <<ChangeStanding bandits -10>>
    Bandit: Wrong answer. #line:shakedown_wrong
===
